		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: New OpenGD77 Beta for TYT MD-9600 / Retevis RT-90]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=3879&amp;p=30168#p30168"><![CDATA[
Hi,<br><br>   That option doesn't exist, I guess you're refereing to <a href="https://github.com/LibreDMR/OpenGD77_UserGuide/blob/master/OpenGD77_User_Guide.md#filter-time" class="postlink">Filter time</a>.<br><br>Short answer, no. Reason is, that would release the TS locking too early, and your transceiver can switch to the other TS way too soon, and mess up the current QSO.<br>I saw you tried to hack the code for this, for even shorter time. Don't expect that will land in the upstream code (default is 10S for a good reason, like don't fight your transceiver because it changed the current TS because the next guy in your current QSO took too much time to hit is PTT key).<br><br>You can still toggle the current TS, with the  <a href="https://github.com/LibreDMR/OpenGD77_UserGuide/blob/master/OpenGD77_User_Guide.md#changing-timeslot-in-dmr-mode" class="postlink">STAR key</a><br><br><br>Cheers<br>---<br>Daniel<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=56">F1RMB</a> — Sun Mar 17, 2024 5:44 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
	</entry>
